<title>SWITZERLAND: Winterthur sets up Austrian pension fund.</title>
<headline>Winterthur sets up Austrian pension fund.</headline>
<dateline>WINTERTHUR, Switzerland 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss insurers Winterthur Group said it had established a pension fund that was open to any firm in Austria following a provisional licence from Austria's finance ministry.</p>
<p>The Winterthur Pension Fund will offer all products permitted under the Austrian pension fund law, Winterthur said in a statement, adding that it saw good opportunities in this area following a careful examination of the market.</p>
<p>It is Winterthur's aim to become one of the leading providers of occupational benefit schemes, it added.</p>
<p>The establishment of the fund is still subject to final approval by the finance ministry.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
